<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
   <meta charset="UTF-8">
   <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
   <title>How It Works - Love Calculator</title>
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="stylesheets/style.css">
</head>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@tailwindcss/browser@4"></script>

<body class="bg-black text-white">

   <!-- Header -->
   <header class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between items-center px-4 sm:px-8 py-4 gap-4">
      <nav>
         <a href="https://mirfeez.github.io/Mirfeez-portfolio" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
            class="text-red-500 font-semibold text-lg">
            Menzi
         </a>
      </nav>

      <a href="/">
         <button class="border border-red-500 px-4 py-2 rounded hover:bg-red-600 transition">
            Back to Calculator
         </button>
      </a>
   </header>

   <!-- Main Section -->
   <main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-2 sm:px-6 lg:px-2 py-10">

      <h1
         class="border-x-4 border-red-500 rounded py-3 text-red-500 text-center text-2xl sm:text-3xl lg:text-4xl mb-6 bg-[#221818] w-full">
         💖 How The Love Calculator Works
      </h1>

      <p class="text-center text-base sm:text-lg mb-10">
         This calculator does <span class="text-red-500 font-semibold">NOT</span> generate random results.
         It uses a character-based compatibility algorithm.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-12">

         <!-- STEP CARD TEMPLATE -->
         <!-- Repeat structure for each step -->

         <div class="border border-zinc-600 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-xl sm:text-2xl p-4">
               Step 1: Combine Both Names
            </h3>

            <div class="relative">
               <img src="/images/1.jpeg" alt="step 1" class="w-full h-auto object-cover">
               <div class="absolute inset-0 shadow-[inset_0_20px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)]"></div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-center p-4 text-sm sm:text-base">
               The two names are joined together and converted to lowercase.
               <br> Example: <strong>Romeo + Juliet → romeojuliet</strong>
            </p>
         </div>

         <!-- Repeat for other steps -->

         <div class="border border-zinc-600 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-xl sm:text-2xl p-4">
               Step 2: Extract Unique Letters
            </h3>

            <div class="relative">
               <img src="/images/2.jpeg" alt="step 2" class="w-full h-auto object-cover">
               <div class="absolute inset-0 shadow-[inset_0_20px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)] "></div>
            </div>

            <p class="text-center p-4 text-sm sm:text-base">
               Only unique alphabetical characters are kept.
               Duplicate letters are ignored.
            </p>
         </div>

         <div class="border border-zinc-600 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-xl sm:text-2xl p-4">Step 3: Count Letter Frequency</h3>
            <div class="relative">
               <img src="/images/3.jpeg" alt="step 3" class=" w-full h-auto object-cover">
               <div class="absolute inset-0 shadow-[inset_0_20px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)] "></div>

            </div>
            <p class="text-center p-4 text-sm sm:text-base">
               Each unique letter is counted based on how many times it
               appears in the combined name.
            </p>
         </div>

         <div class="border border-zinc-600 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-xl sm:text-2xl p-4">Step 4: Pair & Reduce</h3>
            <div class="relative">
               <img src="/images/4.jpeg" alt="step 4" class=" w-full h-auto object-cover">
               <div class="absolute inset-0 shadow-[inset_0_20px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)] "></div>

            </div>
            <p class="text-center p-4 text-sm sm:text-base">
               The first and last numbers are added together repeatedly.
               This process continues until only two digits remain.
            </p>
         </div>

         <div class="border border-zinc-600 rounded-xl overflow-hidden">
            <h3 class="text-red-500 text-xl sm:text-2xl p-4">Step 5: Generate Final Score</h3>
            <div class="relative">
               <img src="/images/5.jpeg" alt="step 5" class=" w-full h-auto object-cover">
               <div class="absolute inset-0 shadow-[inset_0_20px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.8)] "></div>

            </div>
            <p class="text-center p-4 text-sm sm:text-base">
               The final two-digit number becomes the compatibility percentage.
               The same names will always produce the same result. <strong class="text-red-300">As 56%</strong>
            </p>
         </div>

      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 text-center">
         <p class="bg-[#221818] p-6 rounded-xl text-sm sm:text-lg">
            “Love may be <span class="font-bold text-red-500">emotional</span>,
            but here it’s calculated
            <span class="font-bold text-red-500">mathematically.</span> 😁”
         </p>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-10 text-center text-xs sm:text-sm text-red-200">
         ⚠ This calculator is built for fun and entertainment purposes only.
      </p>

   </main>

</body>

</html>